# Reverse proxy: Caddy listens on 443 (public) and forwards to Streamlit,
# which only listens on localhost:8501 (see tooth-review.service) - Caddy is
# the only thing actually exposed to the internet, and it gets Doc Sans a
# real https:// link (auto-issued/renewed Let's Encrypt cert, so her iPad
# shows a normal padlock, not a security warning) with zero manual TLS setup.
#
# Replace with your actual domain/subdomain (see deploy/README.md step 6 for
# where to get one free, e.g. a DuckDNS subdomain pointed at this instance's
# Elastic IP).
your-subdomain.duckdns.org {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8501
}
